   $ex${"titre":"Le regret de Nathan","competence":"argumenter","situation":"Nathan a raté un contrôle. Il raconte sa journée dans son journal, puis discute avec sa mère par messages.","documents":[{"id":"journal","type":"texte","genre":"recit","titre":"Nathan’s diary","blocs":["Last Friday was terrible. I had stayed up late the night before, so I overslept.","When I got to school, the teacher looked at me and said, “You arrived too late.” I wish I had gone to bed earlier! If I had set my alarm, I would have arrived on time."],"source":"Journal écrit pour l’exercice"},{"id":"sms","type":"dialogue","modele":"sms","titre":"Messages de Nathan et Maman","participants":[{"nom":"Nathan","emoji":"👦","cote":"gauche"},{"nom":"Mum","emoji":"👩","cote":"droite"}],"repliques":[{"qui":"Nathan","texte":"I’d studied all week, but I overslept."},{"qui":"Mum","texte":"Oh dear. I’d like to call your teacher."},{"qui":"Nathan","texte":"Please don’t! I’d rather write to her myself."}],"source":"Messages écrits pour l’exercice"}],"questions":[{"enonce":"Touche le mot qui introduit le **regret** de Nathan sur le passé.","aide":"Ce mot est suivi d’un past perfect.","type":"zone","document":"journal","multiple":false},{"enonce":"Que signifie « If I had set my alarm, I would have arrived on time » ?","aide":"La troisième condition parle de ce qui ne s’est pas passé.","type":"choix","options":[{"id":"a","texte":"Il réglera son réveil pour arriver à l’heure."},{"id":"b","texte":"Il n’a pas réglé son réveil et il est arrivé en retard."},{"id":"c","texte":"Il n’a pas réglé son réveil, mais il est arrivé à l’heure."},{"id":"d","texte":"Il a réglé son réveil et il est arrivé à l’heure."}],"multiple":false},{"enonce":"Complète pour rapporter les paroles du professeur.","aide":"Au discours indirect, le prétérit devient un past perfect.","type":"trous","segments":["The teacher said that I ",0," arrived too late."],"banque":["has","was","had","would"]},{"enonce":"Remets en ordre : « S’il avait pris le bus, il serait arrivé plus tôt. » La phrase commence par If he.","aide":"Past perfect dans le *if*, would have + participe dans la principale.","type":"ordre","items":[{"id":"a","texte":"earlier"},{"id":"b","texte":"have arrived"},{"id":"c","texte":"he would"},{"id":"d","texte":"had taken"},{"id":"e","texte":"the bus,"},{"id":"f","texte":"If he"}]},{"enonce":"Dans les messages, ’d vaut-il **had** ou **would** ?","aide":"Après ’d, regarde si le mot suivant est un participe passé.","type":"categories","categories":[{"id":"c0","texte":"’d = had"},{"id":"c1","texte":"’d = would"}],"items":[{"id":"i0","texte":"I’d rather"},{"id":"i1","texte":"I’d like"},{"id":"i2","texte":"I’d studied"}]}]}$ex$::jsonb,
